Subject: Match the registry identity to the landed FIPS source

Bazel requires the fetched MODULE.bazel version to match the registry entry.
Keep the source module's 0.0.3 base version and append its full landed commit,
so SONiC image consumers can select that exact OpenSSL/SymCrypt source through
the registry. Only module identity changes; build rules and dependencies do not.

Provenance: registry-local metadata adjustment to the source declaration at
https://github.com/securely1g/sonic-fips/blob/15fcb926a302059ec379f0c2fd15eb3d88bda4c9/MODULE.bazel#L1-L4
The source commit is the maintained-branch merge of FIPS PR #12, not a new
crypto implementation or an upstream source patch.

--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 module(
     name = "sonic-fips",
-    version = "0.0.3",
+    version = "0.0.3-15fcb926a302059ec379f0c2fd15eb3d88bda4c9",
     bazel_compatibility = [
         ">=8.5.1",
         "<=8.5.1",
